opd: in a replay, read the next step's dump while this one trains.

--load-debug-rollout-data (the replay arms: REPLAY_LOGS on grpo_multi.sh and
opd_multi.sh) reads rollout_<k>.pt in the rollout manager when the driver asks
for step k, unpickles 1536 samples' token and log-prob lists and builds the
Sample objects, then converts and splits them for the trainer. The manager has
nothing else to do in a replay (no engine to drive), and the trainer waits for
it at every step: about 6 s of a 179 s step (perf/train_wait_time on the
MRPD run, 2026-11-07).

So the manager starts reading step k + 1 in a thread as soon as it has handed
out step k; the read overlaps the training of step k, and the next generate()
takes the result. The convert and split of a step stay where they were. A step
asked for out of order (a resume) is read then and there; the step past the
last file is not started; a read that fails raises when its step is taken, as
a synchronous read would. Nothing on the GPU side changes.

Applied by opd_multi.sh when REPLAY_LOGS is set (marker
slime-opd-replay-prefetch); independent of the other patches (rollout.py only).

